From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Lamb <paul@paulscode.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 11:07:05 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Hardening from an adversarial review

- a block that fails to write (a full disk) stops indexing and is retried,
  instead of being skipped for good behind the next block's marker
- start-height and recentblocks written whole (temp file, fsync, rename); a
  damaged recentblocks is read as empty instead of failing every start
- a config.toml that cannot be read stops Frigate with the reason, instead of
  running on defaults against another node and no backend
- the wait for a node behind the index gives up when the node stops advancing
- the fork point search is serialized, a failure remembered per tip, and a
  backend's blake2b_fork passed on only if the node has that block there
- the backend chain check uses the configured TLS, and rechecks every minute
  while it reports another chain
- backfill: cancelled lookups end; wallets rescanned every 10 minutes, not
  every minute; the getblockfrompeer path waits while the node is half again
  over its prune target
- a wallet scanning from below the index's first block is noted in the log
- frigate.log rolls at 10 MB, three old files kept
